    "body": "Sorry for the nitpicking, but two small UX tweaks! \r\nThe first line is more of an explanation than a question, and for input prompts `>` is more natural than `?`:\r\n\r\n```suggestion\r\n        printf \"Where would you like to install Starship? ${GREY}(e.g., /usr/local/bin)${NO_COLOR}\\n\"\r\n        read -p \"> Install Starship ${GREEN}${VERSION}${NO_COLOR} to: \" path\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis creates a cleaner flow:\r\n```\r\n  Where would you like to install Starship? (e.g., /usr/local/bin)\r\n  > Install Starship latest to: |\r\n```",
    "created_at": "2025-08-04T12:10:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-08-04T12:11:43Z",
